Hello,

I have a project regarding cetacean sightings using distance sampling. During the data collection, we also collected weather variables every effort update. These variables I've now managed to add to the dataframe including sightings, observers, cluster size, etc. and I would expect all (or at least some) of these variables (there are 15) such as general sightability, glare, wind speed, beaufort, swell size, and so on to have a considerable effect on the detection function - or at least I would like to see _if_ they have an effect at all.

I would like to make a summary_ds table of all these different models. However, I'm having issues adding these formulae to the model, as the only one working is:

> bal.sz.ds <- ds(fram.var, truncation = 3000, formula = ~size, key = "hr")

when I use the other variables such as:

> bal.obs.ds <- ds(fram.var, truncation = "15%", formula = ~observer, key = "hr")

no models could be fitted!

Is this a problem with the way the variables are formulated? Are number of covariates limited in the formulae? I would love to have:

> bal.mix.ds <- ds(fram.var, truncation = "15%", key = "hr", formula = ~observer + size + weather) #or something of the sort

Thank you for your help!

Hope everyone is healthy in these times,
Elling

