Thanks Steve, this actually makes sense (for a change).

Based on a known CV, I could predict an effect size that could be detected and spread the effect size over multiple years as an annual rate, achieving the known effect size on the last year when compared to the first year.

But I'd also like to get an idea of the power to detect this decline (i.e. include the uncertainty regarding the measurement of the actual abundance). Can I do this as well?

Thanks,
Mitch

